WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.000
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.400
And thank you for --
-Love you, Burna!

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.968
-Yeah, you got
a little love right there.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.167
Since you were last on our show,
you won a Grammy.

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:10.734
Congratulations, bud.
-Thank you.

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:14.701
-That's got to feel good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:17.434
Well, since "Love, Damini"
came out this summer,

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:19.400
the song "Last Last"
was number 1

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.133
on U.S. Afro Beats
chart for eight weeks.

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:23.601
-Hold on. Say it again.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:25.434
-"Love, Damini" or --
-No, the "Last Last."

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.667
-"Last Last" was number 1 --
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:30.234
-Oh, come on. Give me a break.

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:31.534
-It's supposed to be
"Last Last."

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:33.400
-Oh, "Last Last."
-Hey!

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.100
-Sorry. Not...
-With strength.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.234
-..."Last Last."
-No, there's no strength.

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:39.901
-No strength in that.
-"Last Last."

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.267
-"Last Last."
-Hey!

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.901
-Yeah, okay, good.

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:48.601
You're performing "Last Last"
for us later tonight.

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:49.834
-I am.

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:51.767
-You have so many collaborators
on this album.

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:55.801
And I do love J Balvin,
of course.

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:58.300
I know him. Khaled.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.501
Ladysmith Black Mambazo.

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:02.567
And then I see Ed Sheeran.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:05.868
And I go, "Interesting."

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:07.634
Does he know how to pronounce
"Last Last"?

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.667
-Definitely.
-He does, yeah. He does.

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.534
What's Ed Sheeran like when you
get in the studio with him?

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:13.267
-Oh, he's amazing, man.
-He's a good dude.

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.868
-Yeah, he's like one of
my favorite people

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:17.367
in general in the world,
you know?

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:18.601
-Really?
-Yeah, man.

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:21.367
-How did you guys
come about your song?

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:25.033
-Well, the same way we
come about every other song.

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:26.634
-What?
You just get in the studio?

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:28.234
-Yeah, we just literally get
in the studio,

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:30.634
and then it's just
literally magical.

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:35.300
He has a cheat code, 'cause he
plays the guitar the whole time,

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.467
and it's like --

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:38.501
It just makes everything
so much easier, you know?

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:41.667
-Yeah. Where did the name
Burna Boy come from?

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:45.067
-This is weird, but I used to
draw comic books and stuff.

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.234
I know I don't look like it.

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:49.167
But, yeah, I used to
draw comic books and,

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:51.767
like, copy, like, you know,

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:54.000
different, like,
"Spider-Mans" and "Superman."

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.400
I would just draw it.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.467
And then, at a point,
I wanted my own.

00:01:57.467 --> 00:02:01.033
I wanted to be my own superhero,
where I could draw me

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:03.567
as a superhero, you know,
with the cape and all that.

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:05.400
So I was trying to
come up with a name

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.901
and all I could think of
was Burna Boy.

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:08.934
-No way.

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:10.334
So that's where Burna Boy
comes from?

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:12.367
-Literally.
'Cause, you know, Spider-Man...

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:14.567
-Yeah, Spider-Man, Burna Boy.
-Exactly.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:18.868
-Wow! How old were you
when you first started music?

00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:20.767
-[ Breathes deeply ]

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.934
Like 2.

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:24.767
-A baby.
-Yeah.

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:26.100
Like, I could always make music

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.834
and I could always
find my way around music.

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:30.534
-But did you write --
When did you start

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:31.634
really getting into -- 2?

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.033
-No, no, not 2.
-No.

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:35.567
-I used to sing "Hip Hop Hooray"
and stuff when I was young.

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:36.834
-Yeah, of course.

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:38.267
Do you remember
your first song that you wrote?

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.601
-I remember
it was called "Jump,"

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:42.701
and I said "jump"
a bunch of times.

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:46.434
-Yeah. You said that your music
brings people together

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:48.868
who speak different languages,
just through dance.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:53.234
And you -- I was
going to ask you to show me

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.868
a dance move
that maybe I could do.

00:02:55.868 --> 00:03:00.667
If I go to a Burna Boy concert,
I could do it on the stage.

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:03.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
You can teach me how to do it.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:06.200
Just to spread the love,
so we can all --

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.868
Just to spread the love.

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:10.100
-I'm thinking of
an easy one for you.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.501
-Why would you think of
an easy one for me?

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:13.000
You've seen my moves.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.801
-That's exactly why
I'm thinking of an easy one.

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:17.601
[ Laughter, cymbal crash ]

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:20.200
-What can we do?
-Alright. Maybe try this.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.067
I hurt my leg,
so I'm going to --

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:23.200
-Yeah.
♪♪

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.234
Alright, here we go.

00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:25.968
-So, this one is called --

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:28.267
Well, the fans call it
the Afro Moonwalk.

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:29.934
-Afro Moonwalk.
-Yeah.

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:31.968
So, it's almost like
you're walking.

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:33.434
Like, you're walking forward,

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:35.167
but you're not
really moving, right?

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:37.667
-Uh-huh.
-So, you're gonna go like this.

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:46.868
-Here it goes.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:52.400
-At least you didn't fall.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.467
-You do it.
I can do it with you.

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:54.901
Alright, go.

00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:02.234
Burna Boy, everybody.

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:04.267
Check out his album,
"Love, Damini."

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:05.400
It is out now.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.234
He's performing for us
when we come back.

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:09.467
"Last Last"!
Stick around, everybody.

